# Day 29 — deny-by-default allow-list.
# The manifest in docs/deployment.yaml is the source of truth for what ships.
# An exclusion list is a list of things someone remembered; the failure mode of
# forgetting is silent and irreversible in a layer. An allow-list fails loud:
# a new file is excluded by default and shows up in N1 as a context path with
# no reason.

# Deny everything by default
*

# Allow only the manifest's include set (paths relative to repo root)
!ai_os/
!tools/
!policy.yaml
!.env.example
!requirements.txt
!data/store.json

# Explicit non-size exclusions (named because they are the ones that matter)
.env
.git/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
*.pem
.netrc
.aws/
data/*
!data/store.json